  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal and literary verb. Also written {讃|たた}える. More elevated than {褒|ほ}める (to praise — everyday, casual). {称|たた}える implies public recognition or deep respect, while {褒|ほ}める is used for everyday compliments.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {功績|こうせき}を{称|たた}える: to honor achievements\n- {勇気|ゆうき}を{称|たた}える: to praise courage\n- ～を{称|たた}えて: in honor of...\n- {互|たが}いの{健闘|けんとう}を{称|たた}え{合|あ}う: to commend each other's efforts",
